# Screenshot originals. `npm run shots` converts these to .webp, which is what
# the site actually serves — committing multi-megabyte PNGs alongside would
# bloat the repo permanently, since git history keeps them even after deletion.
# Keep the originals locally so the optimizer can be re-run.
public/shots/*.png
public/shots/*.jpg
public/shots/*.jpeg
.env*

# Claude Code local settings. Accumulates whatever tool permissions you grant
# over time and is named .local because it is per-machine — it should never be
# world-readable in a public repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
